h equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2t \\\\ y=5+t \\\\ z=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x+3y-4z=-43.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+3y-4z & =-43 \\\\ 5(6+2t)+3(5+t)-4(-3-3t) & =-43 \\\\ 30+10t+15+3t+12+12t & =-43 \\\\ 25t & =-100 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=6+2(-4) \\\\ y=5+(-4) \\\\ z=-3-3(-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-2,1,9).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108326/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108326"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108323/selection/2f3525db4fe135d9cde691a52e2de5c88fd72ebfd771f4d19da0145b8825ae78" :answer/id #uuid "39aba5e9-0c9f-540f-b74d-16c2a40e488a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(11,5,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108323/selection/3e8c27bfed9319558f72d499a00ef898b6630a5597323e726909b66ce6db3406" :answer/id #uuid "4a8b0c89-d047-564c-bd0f-7be376601439" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,0,4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108323/selection/86674c3f27c84ba4a504138abd8e394ed418c8a0d4445a9b47946a02a989b688" :answer/id #uuid "354ae279-9213-5947-a40b-84a3fdcefc17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108323/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "ff97cc03-27a1-58d6-8889-d7dde92b0edb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108323/selection/730dbe5cc596fbf22a49cfe5f80a636c0ac880e0c6e82eac791