:db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108337" :question/id #uuid "36683b19-26fd-5526-a537-6298e5ac4183" :question/math-academy-id "q-108337" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3t \\\\ y=5+2t \\\\ z=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108337/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108337"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33194/selection/45aae12f3cdd45c15a708919735dafe5118da281e47822a762b3ca0b85aa2116" :answer/id #uuid "ba3d75a8-d756-5a68-b38b-92b969430fa8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33194/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "0c958dd1-085a-5ae3-b8e0-7faec2e6a810" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33194/selection/e8a39d298245faf0419c3a6fb1f72267e3504eda0a33f486994aa93f48f43f20" :answer/id #uuid "d0d71fc4-41cf-5be8-b326-95b9f8e7974f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-5,0,-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33194/selection/b7b22ca4a49946995324ecd2884533dc4ef34d9afa4c35917eb5ce0