y, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33194/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33194"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "bbfef096-0506-51a2-91cc-3d099bc1c06d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205/selection/8fb8899aadb75cdd69c5f629750dd77b2f1cab4e7c70efc08ac756ff829ea9a0" :answer/id #uuid "42d6c4ce-4668-5bee-bc85-f8090d692fc6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205/selection/f5be1b3afe3e43ba781161ee7076381a1fb728d235e6305bbcca2199a7031ab7" :answer/id #uuid "7391d614-f965-5593-97fd-d62ce5d9eb1c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(14,8,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205/selection/653d6af4c857a9be28768ec817797b5efdd25da66650a92a696d4332dc1dfe4e" :answer/id #uuid "42436bde-7a95-5fd0-8e7e-17a262ce6c77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,8,14)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205/selection/ddac6e912ea8f814d7ae1df63446db24e30987706ddf384ce1cfbaacb0465ee1" :answer/id #uuid "0a291b95-adc1-50e4-a3c9-74dbc1d576c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,4,8)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e21fd410-8d68-5c04-9351-bb619c018421" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33205/selection/653d6af4c857a9be28768ec817797b5efdd25da66650a92a696d4332dc1dfe4e" :answer-field/choices ["q-33205/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-33205/selection/8fb8899aadb75cdd69c5f629750dd77b2f1cab4e7c70efc08ac756ff829ea9a0" "q-33205/selection/f5be1b3afe3e43ba781161ee7076381a1fb728d235e6305bbcca2199a7031ab7" "q-33205/selection/653d6af4c857a9be28768ec817797b5efdd25da66650a92a696d4332dc1dfe4e" "q-33205/selection/ddac6e912ea8f814d7ae1df63446db24e30987706ddf384ce1cfbaacb0465ee1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33205" :question/id #uuid "eaab1f60-24fb-5572-8cfb-474f418bf09f" :question/math-academy-id "q-33205" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,-2,6⟩+t⟨2,5,4⟩,\\,Π:x+2y+z-33=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z-33 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z & =33 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ ⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ -1+2t+2(-2+5t)+6+4t & =33 \\\\ -1+2t-4+10t+6+4t & =33 \\\\ 16t & =32 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+2(2),-2+5(2),6+4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,8,14⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(3,8,14).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33205/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33205"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33201/selection/59e8665f2579f89535f0d8c21270fc85ffa7812cedbfe5633314dfc241e50fbb" :answer/id #u